Complete proxy: bias of a rate defined on absolute correlations
  sigma(r_net) = 0.0218 (empirical over R replicates)
  |r_base|     = 0.3214 (population value, not a single draw)
  predicted E[lambda] = 1 - (2/pi)^0.5 * sigma / |r_base| = 0.9459
  recovered = 0.9458 ; gap = -0.0001 against a Monte Carlo s.e. of 0.0013,
  so the departure from 1.0000 is definitional, not simulation noise.
  Section 5.6 of the paper reports it rather than hiding it.

